    native_c_runtime_missing_cuda_provider_forwarders_2026-11-22, P3, verified, "Native C runtime has no forwarders for 28 CUDA externs; native programs using std device queries fail to link (2026-11-22)", doc/08_tracking/bug/native_c_runtime_missing_cuda_provider_forwarders_2026-11-22.md, 1, doc/08_tracking/bug/native_c_runtime_missing_cuda_provider_forwarders_2026-11-22.md, 2026-11-22, 2026-11-26, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    native_c_runtime_missing_cuda_provider_forwarders_2026-11-22, 0, "2026-11-26 work/bug-cuda-native-20261126: runtime_dynload.c forwards 27 of the 28 externs, with sentinels equal to the Rust non-cuda twins. device_name is copied into a per-thread runtime-owned buffer while pinned. A first call that lands in LOADING now spins until the loader finishes. get_error_string is a pure C copy of the Rust table. Gap: cuda_module_get_function_cstr_text_abi_2026-11-26. Red: the Stage 2 link had 4 undefined symbols, and the registry check showed undefined symbols, then race=0,3 and name_owned=0. Green: the registry check passes. check-cuda-device-query-native.shs PASS on a GB10 (gpu, no provider, missing libcuda; C and Rust lanes identical). The std gpu_ops probe (cuda_std_device_query_probe.spl) reports NVIDIA GB10 12.1."

